# What EAS Build does NOT need in the project archive.
#
# This file has to live at the repository root, not in apps/mobile: EAS
# archives from the git root in a monorepo (so workspace dependencies resolve),
# and it reads the ignore rules from that same root. An .easignore inside
# apps/mobile is simply never consulted, which is why the first attempt changed
# nothing and every upload was ~430 MB and eight minutes.
#
# Note that .easignore REPLACES .gitignore for archiving. Anything that must
# stay out has to be listed here even though git already ignores it -- and
# anything the build genuinely needs must NOT be listed, even if git ignores
# it.

# Dependencies: reinstalled on the builder from the lockfiles.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# The merchant portal is a separate Next.js app that no mobile build touches.
apps/merchant/

# Expo and build output.
.expo/
**/.expo/
dist/
**/dist/
web-build/
**/web-build/

# Native projects are generated by prebuild on the builder; a stale local copy
# is worse than none.
android/
ios/
**/android/
**/ios/

# Secrets and local config. Build-time values live in EAS environment
# variables (eas env:list) rather than in the archive -- see the notes in
# docs/MOBILE_SETUP.md. google-services.json is deliberately NOT ignored: the
# Android build reads it from the archive.
.env
**/.env
.env.local
**/.env.local

# Artefacts and local noise.
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
coverage/

# Supabase migrations are applied with the CLI, not by the app.
supabase/
